hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15518","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr and Surayj, in meaning, both said: Nafi ibn Umar narrated to us, from Umayyah ibn Safwan, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Zuhayr, my father said: Both of them said: From Abu Bakr ibn Abi Zuhayr al-Thaqafi, from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying at al-Nabaah, or at al-Nibawah, Nafi doubted, of al-Taif, and he was saying: O people, you are soon to know the people of Paradise from the people of Fire, or he said: Your best from your worst, he said: Then a man of the people said: By what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: By evil praise and good praise, and you are the witnesses of Allah, some of you over others."
